In article <nwang.716745713@black.clarku.edu> nwang@black.clarku.edu (Anonymous) writes:

More spoilers a-comin:

>1) Do I really need 2 pets?  I now have both a large cat and a small
>dog, it's kinda nice to have them help me but getting them downstais is
>a pain.

You don't *need* any pets.  They *can* be quite useful, both to your survival
and to your final score.  Especially if they get 'morfed.

Think of Mae West:  Put your lips together and blow.  If that doesn't work,
try an artificial aid to the same purpose.


>2) I have a ring a levitation, can the monsters still attack me?  And
>what kind of traps can I avoid?

All but the very shortest monsters can attack you.  You can avoid a lot of
traps, especially the very nastiest (imio), the land mine.


>3) After praying once, I offered a couple of corpse to my altar, the
>message were "The corpse disappears in flame" or something, what does
>that suppose to mean?

It means the deity has accepted your offering.  It doesn't mean the deity
is doing anything about it.  Look for something small and green.


>4) I also have a pick-axe, 2 magic markers (what are they good for?) and
>a mirror, how should I use them.

Two magic markers?  Marvellous!  You write with them, of course; (a)pply them
to a blank scroll.  You can also avoid ravaging monsters for a while, if you
know your Tolkien and remember how to spell the name of the star-Lady.


>And last, can I eat green mold corpse?

Sure.  But I hope you've got some Tums.


